.TH MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_notify \- Python publisher library for the Mu2e DAQ notification server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from mu2edaq_notify import NotifyPublisher, publish_event
.B from mu2edaq_notify import SEVERITIES, normalize_event, severity_index

pub = NotifyPublisher(server_url=None, token=None, source=None,
                      category=None, host=None, timeout=5.0,
                      discover=True, fallback_url=None)
ok = pub.publish(severity, title, message="", source=None,
                 category=None, meta=None)
pub.debug(title, message="", **kw)      pub.info(...)
pub.warning(...)    pub.error(...)      pub.critical(...)

ok = publish_event(severity, title, message="", **kwargs)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standard\-library\-only client that publishes one event per call to
.B POST /api/events
on
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1).
Installing the
.B mu2edaq-notify
distribution nevertheless pulls in the server's dependencies (Flask,
SQLAlchemy, httpx, cryptography), because they are declared as package
dependencies.
.PP
.B Address resolution.
The constructor resolves two addresses, each in the order argument >
environment > discovery: the primary
.RB ( server_url ,
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL ,
then the first mu2edaq\-discovery ANNOUNCE for
.BR app=notify )
and the fallback
.RB ( fallback_url ,
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL ,
then that ANNOUNCE's
.BR meta.fallback_url ).
Discovery runs once, inside the constructor, only when
.B discover
is true, either address is still unset, and
.B mu2edaq_discovery
is importable. The result is never refreshed: a publisher constructed while
the server is unreachable or not announcing keeps no address, and every later
.B publish()
returns False after one WARNING log line. Long\-running processes should pass
.B server_url
explicitly or construct the publisher when they publish.
.PP
.B Delivery.
.B publish()
POSTs to the primary and tries the fallback only when the primary cannot be
reached at the network level (DNS, connection, timeout, TLS); any HTTP reply,
including 4xx and 5xx, ends the attempt. It returns True on a 2xx reply and
False otherwise, and logs failures at WARNING through the
.B mu2edaq_notify.publisher
logger. It does not raise on a delivery failure. It
.B does
raise
.B ValueError
when both
.I title
and
.I message
are empty, because the event is normalized client\-side before sending.
.PP
.B Credentials.
The bearer token is sent to whichever address is used. An address learned
from discovery comes from an unauthenticated multicast reply, so a host on
the same subnet can direct the token to itself; pass
.B server_url
explicitly where that matters. HTTPS is verified against
.B certifi
when installed, else the system CA store.
.PP
.B Thread safety.
A publisher holds no mutable state after construction and may be shared
between threads; each call opens its own connection.
.SH "EVENT FIELDS"
.B publish()
builds the event with
.BR normalize_event ():
.TP
.B severity
One of
.BR SEVERITIES :
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warning ,
.BR error ,
.BR critical ,
case\-insensitive. Any other value is silently replaced by
.BR info .
.TP
.BR title ", " message
Title up to 200 characters, message up to 4000; an empty title becomes the
first line of the message.
.TP
.BR source ", " category
Per\-call value, else the publisher's own (constructor argument; for
.B source
the basename of
.BR $_ ,
else
.BR python ;
for
.B category
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY ,
else empty). Both truncated to 100 characters. Categories are freeform; the
server's
.B GET /api/categories
lists the configured set but does not enforce it.
.TP
.B host
The constructor's
.BR host ,
else
.BR socket.gethostname ().
.TP
.B meta
A dict; keys and values are converted with
.BR str ().
No size limit is applied.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL
Primary server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL
Fallback server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN
Publisher bearer token.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY
Default category.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
import logging, os
from mu2edaq_notify import NotifyPublisher

log = logging.getLogger(__name__)

pub = NotifyPublisher(server_url="https://mu2edaq\-pager.fnal.gov",
                      token=os.environ["MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN"],
                      source="dtc\-monitor", category="Trigger")
if not pub.error("DTC link down", "ROC link 3 lost lock",
                 meta={"run": "107001"}):
    log.warning("page not accepted")
.fi
